{
  "id": "oculomotor-palsy",
  "term": "oculomotor palsy",
  "definition": "Oculomotor palsy is a disorder of the third cranial nerve or its brain nucleus that causes weakness or paralysis of muscles controlling eye movement and eyelid lifting, and may also reduce the nerve supply that constricts the pupil. In a complete palsy, the eyelid droops, the eye rests turned outward and downward, and the pupil is greatly enlarged.",
